    "updated_at": "2026-11-25T14:48:01Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/2829-flow-multiband · PR #4018 · pinned by rotary_flow band laws (three_ordered_chains_cut_two_bands_and_the_boundary_once, one_helical_chain_covers_the_full_revolution, a_ring_that_crosses_a_corner_chain_is_refused_by_name), the rotary_flow unit refusal pins (meet at the spot, backtrack, lap morph), and the app pins (three_ring_chains_cut_two_bands_and_the_boundary_once, one_meridian_chain_machines_the_full_revolution, a_pick_set_whose_chains_meet_is_refused_by_name) · merges at the next cut\n\nFindings from the work, for the record:\n\n- The #2824 opposite-sense refusal is superseded: the feature layer reads a chain's direction from the mesh, never from the pick (the end-face rings of the bar extract wound -TAU while the profile rings extract +TAU), so a chain wound against its pair is now walked backwards, said in the notes. The raw pairing of two oppositely wound chains twists the band a whole turn; the reversal untwists it.\n- A developed-offset fold refusal was drafted and dropped the same day: the #2824 box band pins a lens-shaped band (the offset pinches through zero at the axis-nearest place) as legal, so the band direction is read as a mean only, and only the 3-D meet/cross law and the backtrack law refuse.\n- The app band picks' old test helper selected the shoulder cone's 72 meridian edge chains alongside the two rings (the old kernel machined 73 sliver bands there); the helper now selects ring chains only, and the new laws refuse the old garbage set by name.\n- The lap band's two edges are one world curve: the closing pass is dropped, the picked chain emits once.\n- The quick gate's app prebuild wedged once (#3675) and the planned app suites ran one by one: all green. The light lane's all-binaries release build failed on machine disk during the run, not on code; the substantive light twins ran green.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
