    "updated_at": "2026-11-25T16:34:44Z",
    "body": "The PR #4018 review (mkinney, 2026-11-25) found two blocking defects. Both are fixed on the same branch and pushed (head 99283bc76): the complete guide set is normalized once before the bands are cut, and the azimuth-only single guide - a closed ring or an open arc - is refused by name. The \"Addressed\" comment on PR #4018 states the readings.\n\nThe review's non-blocking finding - a crossing between non-adjacent guide chains passes, on main and on the PR head - is filed as #4032 and stays out of this branch.\n",
